/-!
# Complements on the subscheme cut out by an ideal sheaf

This file adds two independent complements to `Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Subscheme`.

## Base change of the subscheme cut out by an ideal sheaf

The affine cover of the closed subscheme `V(I)` cut out by a quasi-coherent ideal `I` is
obtained by base change: over an affine open `U` of `X`, the square formed by the chart
`Spec (Γ(X, U) ⧸ I(U)) ⟶ V(I)` of `I.subschemeCover`, the closed immersion `I.subschemeι`
and `U.2.fromSpec` is a pullback
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isPullback_subschemeCover_map`).

Pasting this square with `Spec` of the pushout square `CommRingCat.isPushout_quotient`
computes the base change of `I.subschemeι` along an arbitrary affine probe
`Spec.map φ ≫ U.2.fromSpec`: it is the closed immersion cut out by the extended ideal
`I(U)·S` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isPullback_subschemeι_specMap_fromSpec`).

## The map to the scheme-theoretic image is scheme-theoretically dominant

For a quasi-compact `f : X ⟶ Y`, Mathlib factors `f` as `f.toImage ≫ f.imageι` through the
scheme-theoretic image, and knows that `f.toImage` is dominant and quasi-compact. It does not
record that `f.toImage` is *scheme-theoretically* dominant, which is the stronger statement
that makes the image the smallest closed subscheme through which `f` factors. This file adds
it, in the form `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_toImage : f.toImage.ker = ⊥`.

The proof is the expected one and uses no new input: `f.toImage.app` is injective over the
preimage of an affine open of `Y` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.toImage_app_injective`), those
preimages are affine because `f.imageι` is a closed immersion, and they cover the image, so
the kernel ideal vanishes on a cover by affine opens.

## The scheme-theoretic closure of a dense open subscheme

Let `U` be a dense open subscheme of a scheme `X` whose inclusion is quasi-compact, and let
`X* := U.ι.image` be the scheme-theoretic image of `U ⟶ X`, the smallest closed subscheme of
`X` through which `U` factors. Then `X* ⟶ X` is a surjective closed immersion which is an
isomorphism over `U`, and `U` is a *scheme-theoretically* dense open subscheme of `X*`. This is
step 2 of the proof of Chow's lemma (blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure`): it
replaces `X` by a scheme in which `U` is scheme-theoretically dense.

Surjectivity holds for the scheme-theoretic image of any dominant quasi-compact morphism, since
the underlying set of the scheme-theoretic image is the closure of the set-theoretic image
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.range_imageι`). That `X* ⟶ X` is an isomorphism over `U` comes
from the identification of the open `U ⊆ X*` with the preimage of `U ⊆ X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.opensRange_toImage`), and the scheme-theoretic density of `U`
in `X*` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_toImage` transported along that identification.

## The subscheme cut out by an ideal sheaf inherits quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness

The inclusion `I.subschemeι` is a closed immersion, hence affine, so `V(I)` is quasi-compact
(resp. quasi-separated) as soon as the ambient scheme is.

## The reduced induced subscheme structure

The subscheme cut out by the vanishing ideal of a closed subset `Z` is reduced: on an affine open
`U` it is `Spec (Γ(X, U) ⧸ I)` for a radical ideal `I`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isReduced_subscheme_vanishingIdeal`). Applied to
the closure of a point of height one, it shows that a scheme of finite positive dimension has a
closed subscheme of dimension one
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isClosedImmersion_topologicalKrullDim_eq_one`).

## The closed subscheme cut out by global sections

The closed subscheme `V(s)` cut out by a set `s` of global sections is the subscheme of the
ideal sheaf generated by `s` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zeroLocusSubscheme`). Its underlying set
is the zero locus of `s` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.range_zeroLocusSubschemeι`), the
complement of the basic open `X_f` when `s = {f}`. The sections of `s` vanish on `V(s)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zeroLocusSubschemeι_appTop`), and a quasi-compact morphism on which
they vanish factors through `V(s)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.liftZeroLocusSubscheme`).

## Morphisms from reduced schemes

A morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` from a reduced scheme kills the nilradical of `Y`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.nilradical_le_ker`), hence factors through the reduced closed
subscheme `Y.nilradical.subscheme` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.liftNilradical`).

## Main results

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isPullback_subschemeCover_map`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isPullback_subschemeι_specMap_fromSpec`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.isReduced_subscheme_vanishingIdeal`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.exists_isClosedImmersion_topologicalKrullDim_eq_one`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zeroLocusSubscheme` and its closed immersion
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zeroLocusSubschemeι`, with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.range_zeroLocusSubschemeι`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zeroLocusSubschemeι_appTop` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.liftZeroLocusSubscheme`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.ker_toImage`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.nilradical_le_ker` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.liftNilradical`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.closedComplement` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.range_closedComplement`, with the specialisations
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.closedComplement` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.range_closedComplement` to the range of an open immersion
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.range_imageι` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.surjective_imageι`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.isIso_morphismRestrict_imageι`
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_preimage_imageι`
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens)

/-- The affine chart of the subscheme over an affine open is the fibre product: the
square with the chart `Spec (Γ(X, U) ⧸ I(U)) ⟶ V(I)` and `fromSpec` is a pullback. -/
lemma isPullback_subschemeCover_map :
    IsPullback (I.subschemeCover.f U)
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I.ideal U))))
      I.subschemeι U.2.fromSpec := by
  refine (IsOpenImmersion.isPullback _ _ _ _ ?_ ?_).flip
  · exact (I.subschemeCover_map_subschemeι U).trans (I.glueDataObjι_ι U)
  · rw [U.2.opensRange_fromSpec, opensRange_subschemeCover_map]

/-- **The subscheme of an ideal sheaf base changes to the subscheme of the extended
ideal.** Along a morphism `Spec S ⟶ X` of the form `Spec.map φ ≫ U.2.fromSpec` with `U` an
affine open, the base change of `I.subschemeι` is `Spec` of the quotient of `S` by the
extension of `I(U)` along `φ`. -/
lemma isPullback_subschemeι_specMap_fromSpec {S : CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : Γ(X, U.1) ⟶ S) :
    IsPullback (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.quotientMap ((I.ideal U).map φ.hom) φ.hom
        Ideal.le_comap_map)) ≫ I.subschemeCover.f U)
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk ((I.ideal U).map φ.hom))))
      I.subschemeι (Spec.map φ ≫ U.2.fromSpec) :=
  (isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout _ _ _ _
    (CommRingCat.isPushout_quotient φ (I.ideal U))).paste_horiz
      (I.isPullback_subschemeCover_map U)

instance compactSpace_subscheme [CompactSpace X] : CompactSpace I.subscheme :=
  QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace I.subschemeι

instance quasiSeparatedSpace_subscheme [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] :
    QuasiSeparatedSpace I.subscheme :=
  quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated I.subschemeι

/-- The subscheme cut out by the vanishing ideal of a closed subset is reduced: this is the
reduced induced subscheme structure on the closed subset. -/
instance isReduced_subscheme_vanishingIdeal (Z : TopologicalSpace.Closeds X) :
    IsReduced (vanishingIdeal Z).subscheme := by
  have (U : X.affineOpens) : IsReduced ((vanishingIdeal Z).subschemeCover.openCover.X U) := by
    have : _root_.IsReduced (Γ(X, U) ⧸ (vanishingIdeal Z).ideal U) :=
      (Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced _).mp (PrimeSpectrum.isRadical_vanishingIdeal _)
    exact inferInstanceAs (IsReduced (Spec (.of (Γ(X, U) ⧸ (vanishingIdeal Z).ideal U))))
  exact IsReduced.of_openCover _ (vanishingIdeal Z).subschemeCover.openCover

/-- The inclusions of the subschemes attached to equal ideal sheaves agree up to
`eqToHom`. -/
lemma eqToHom_comp_subschemeι {I J : X.IdealSheafData} (e : I = J) :
    eqToHom (congrArg Scheme.IdealSheafData.subscheme e) ≫ J.subschemeι = I.subschemeι := by
  subst e
  simp

/-- The closed subscheme cut out by a set `s` of global sections has the zero locus of `s` as
underlying set. -/
lemma range_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_span (s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    Set.range (ofIdealTop (Ideal.span s)).subschemeι.base = X.zeroLocus s := by
  simp [range_subschemeι, coe_support_ofIdealTop, Scheme.zeroLocus_span]

/-- A global section whose restrictions to the affine opens lie in `I` vanishes on the closed
subscheme cut out by `I`. -/
lemma subschemeι_appTop_eq_zero (t : Γ(X, ⊤))
    (ht : ∀ U : X.affineOpens, X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op t ∈ I.ideal U) :
    I.subschemeι.appTop t = 0 := by
  refine Scheme.zero_of_zero_cover (𝒰 := I.subschemeCover.openCover) _ fun U ↦ ?_
  change ((I.subschemeCover.f U ≫ I.subschemeι).appTop) t = 0
  rw [I.subschemeCover_map_subschemeι, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, CommRingCat.comp_apply,
    ← RingHom.mem_ker, I.ker_glueDataObjι_appTop, Ideal.mem_comap]
  simpa only [Scheme.Opens.topIso_hom, Scheme.Hom.appTop, Scheme.Opens.ι_app,
    ← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp, Subsingleton.elim _ (homOfLE le_top).op]
    using ht U

/-- The ideal sheaf generated by global sections `s` is contained in the kernel of every
quasi-compact morphism on which the sections of `s` vanish. -/
lemma ofIdealTop_span_le_ker {Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X) [QuasiCompact f] {s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)}
    (hs : ∀ t ∈ s, f.appTop t = 0) : ofIdealTop (Ideal.span s) ≤ f.ker := by
  intro U
  rw [ofIdealTop_ideal, Scheme.Hom.ker_apply, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap, Ideal.span_le]
  intro t ht
  simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
  rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, Scheme.Hom.naturality, CommRingCat.comp_apply,
    show f.app ⊤ t = 0 from hs t ht, map_zero]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- A scheme of finite positive dimension has a closed subscheme of dimension one: the reduced
induced subscheme structure on the closure of a point of height one. -/
theorem exists_isClosedImmersion_topologicalKrullDim_eq_one {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (h1 : 1 ≤ topologicalKrullDim X) (htop : topologicalKrullDim X ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ (C : Scheme.{u}) (i : C ⟶ X), IsClosedImmersion i ∧ topologicalKrullDim C = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := exists_topologicalKrullDim_closure_singleton_eq_one h1 htop
  let I := IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {z}, isClosed_closure⟩
  refine ⟨I.subscheme, I.subschemeι, inferInstance, ?_⟩
  have hr : Set.range I.subschemeι = closure {z} := by
    rw [IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]
    rfl
  rw [← hz]
  exact IsHomeomorph.topologicalKrullDim_eq _
    ((I.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.isEmbedding.toHomeomorph.trans
      (Homeomorph.setCongr hr)).isHomeomorph)

variable (X : Scheme.{u})

/-- The closed subscheme `V(s)` of `X` cut out by a set `s` of global sections: the subscheme of
the ideal sheaf generated by `s`. -/
noncomputable abbrev zeroLocusSubscheme (s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)) : Scheme.{u} :=
  (IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span s)).subscheme

/-- The closed immersion `V(s) ⟶ X` of the closed subscheme cut out by a set `s` of global
sections. -/
noncomputable abbrev zeroLocusSubschemeι (s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)) : X.zeroLocusSubscheme s ⟶ X :=
  (IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.span s)).subschemeι

variable {X}

/-- The underlying set of `V(s)` is the zero locus of `s`. -/
lemma range_zeroLocusSubschemeι (s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι s).base = X.zeroLocus s :=
  IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_span s

/-- The closed subscheme `V(f)` and the basic open `X_f` are complementary. -/
lemma range_zeroLocusSubschemeι_singleton (f : Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι {f}).base = (Set.range (X.basicOpen f).ι.base)ᶜ := by
  rw [range_zeroLocusSubschemeι, Scheme.Opens.range_ι, Scheme.zeroLocus_singleton]

/-- `V(insert a s) = V(a) ∩ V(s)`. -/
lemma range_zeroLocusSubschemeι_insert (a : Γ(X, ⊤)) (s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)) :
    Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι (insert a s)).base =
      Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι {a}).base ∩ Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι s).base := by
  simp only [range_zeroLocusSubschemeι, Scheme.zeroLocus_insert]

/-- The closed subscheme cut out by no sections is everything. -/
lemma range_zeroLocusSubschemeι_empty :
    Set.range (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι ∅).base = Set.univ := by
  rw [range_zeroLocusSubschemeι, Scheme.zeroLocus_empty_eq_univ]

/-- The sections cutting out `V(s)` vanish on it. -/
lemma zeroLocusSubschemeι_appTop {s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)} {t : Γ(X, ⊤)} (ht : t ∈ s) :
    (X.zeroLocusSubschemeι s).appTop t = 0 :=
  IdealSheafData.subschemeι_appTop_eq_zero _ t fun _ ↦
    Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span ht)

/-- A quasi-compact morphism on which the sections `s` vanish factors through `V(s)`. -/
noncomputable def Hom.liftZeroLocusSubscheme {Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X) [QuasiCompact f]
    {s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)} (hs : ∀ t ∈ s, f.appTop t = 0) : Y ⟶ X.zeroLocusSubscheme s :=
  f.toImage ≫ IdealSheafData.inclusion (IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_span_le_ker f hs)

@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma Hom.liftZeroLocusSubscheme_zeroLocusSubschemeι {Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    [QuasiCompact f] {s : Set Γ(X, ⊤)} (hs : ∀ t ∈ s, f.appTop t = 0) :
    f.liftZeroLocusSubscheme hs ≫ X.zeroLocusSubschemeι s = f := by
  simp [Hom.liftZeroLocusSubscheme]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)

/-- The kernel of the map to the scheme-theoretic image is trivial: no closed subscheme of
`f.image` strictly smaller than `f.image` contains the image of `f`. -/
lemma ker_toImage [QuasiCompact f] : f.toImage.ker = ⊥ := by
  refine IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top
    (fun V : Y.affineOpens ↦ ⟨f.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ V.1, V.2.preimage f.imageι⟩) ?_ fun V ↦ ?_
  · rw [← preimage_iSup, iSup_affineOpens_eq_top, preimage_top]
  · rw [ker_apply]
    exact (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp (f.toImage_app_injective V)

instance [QuasiCompact f] : IsSchemeTheoreticallyDominant f.toImage := ⟨f.ker_toImage⟩

/-- The underlying set of the scheme-theoretic image of a quasi-compact morphism is the
closure of the set-theoretic image. -/
lemma range_imageι [QuasiCompact f] :
    Set.range f.imageι = closure (Set.range f) := by
  rw [IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, f.support_ker]

/-- The scheme-theoretic image of a dominant quasi-compact morphism is the whole target: the
closed immersion `f.imageι` is surjective.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (1)) -/
instance surjective_imageι [QuasiCompact f] [IsDominant f] : Surjective f.imageι :=
  ⟨Set.range_eq_univ.mp <| by rw [range_imageι, f.denseRange.closure_range]⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (U : X.Opens)

/-- The **closed complement** of an open `U ⊆ X`: the closed subscheme of `X` cut out by the
vanishing ideal of the closed set `Uᶜ`. -/
noncomputable def closedComplement :
    (IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal ⟨(U : Set X)ᶜ, U.isOpen.isClosed_compl⟩).subscheme ⟶ X :=
  IdealSheafData.subschemeι _

instance isClosedImmersion_closedComplement : IsClosedImmersion U.closedComplement :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsClosedImmersion (IdealSheafData.subschemeι _))

/-- The closed complement of an open `U` is supported exactly on the complement of `U`. -/
@[simp]
lemma range_closedComplement : Set.range U.closedComplement.base = (U : Set X)ᶜ := by
  simp [closedComplement, IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι,
    IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]

section

variable [QuasiCompact U.ι]

/-- The scheme-theoretic closure `X*` of a dense open `U ⊆ X` maps onto `X`.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (1)) -/
lemma surjective_imageι_ι (hU : Dense (U : Set X)) : Surjective U.ι.imageι :=
  have : IsDominant U.ι := ⟨by rwa [DenseRange, range_ι]⟩
  inferInstance

/-- The copy of `U` inside the scheme-theoretic image `X*` of `U ⟶ X` is the preimage of `U`:
the open immersion `U ⟶ X*` has image `X* ∩ U`. -/
@[simp]
lemma opensRange_toImage : U.ι.toImage.opensRange = U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
  refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.ext ?_
  have h : (U : Set X) = U.ι.imageι '' Set.range U.ι.toImage := by
    rw [← Set.range_comp, ← TopCat.coe_comp, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_base, U.ι.toImage_imageι, range_ι]
  change Set.range U.ι.toImage = U.ι.imageι ⁻¹' (U : Set X)
  rw [h, Set.preimage_image_eq _ U.ι.imageι.isClosedEmbedding.injective]

/-- The scheme-theoretic closure `X* ⟶ X` of an open `U ⊆ X` is an isomorphism over `U`.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (1)) -/
instance isIso_morphismRestrict_imageι : IsIso (U.ι.imageι ∣_ U) := by
  -- `U.ι.toImage` corestricts to an isomorphism `e : U ≅ X* ∩ U`, ...
  set e := U.ι.toImage.isoOpensRange ≪≫ U.ι.image.isoOfEq (opensRange_toImage U) with he
  -- ... and `e` is a section of the restriction `X* ∩ U ⟶ U` of `X* ⟶ X`.
  have hcomp : e.hom ≫ (U.ι.imageι ∣_ U) = 𝟙 _ := by
    rw [← cancel_mono U.ι, Category.assoc, morphismRestrict_ι, Category.id_comp, he]
    simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Category.assoc, Scheme.isoOfEq_hom_ι_assoc,
      Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_hom_ι_assoc, Scheme.Hom.toImage_imageι]
  have : IsIso (e.hom ≫ (U.ι.imageι ∣_ U)) := hcomp ▸ inferInstance
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_left e.hom _

/-- **`U` is scheme-theoretically dense in its scheme-theoretic closure `X*`**: the inclusion
of the copy of `U` in `X*` is scheme-theoretically dominant.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (2)) -/
instance isSchemeTheoreticallyDominant_preimage_imageι :
    IsSchemeTheoreticallyDominant (U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ U).ι := by
  rw [← opensRange_toImage U, ← Scheme.Hom.isoOpensRange_inv_comp U.ι.toImage]
  infer_instance

end

/-- The trace on `X*` of an affine open of `X` is affine, since `X* ⟶ X` is a closed immersion.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (3)) -/
lemma isAffineOpen_preimage_imageι {V : X.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    IsAffineOpen (U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ V) :=
  hV.preimage U.ι.imageι

/-- The traces on `X*` of an open covering of `X` cover `X*`.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (3)) -/
lemma iSup_preimage_imageι_eq_top {ι : Type*} {V : ι → X.Opens} (hV : ⨆ i, V i = ⊤) :
    ⨆ i, U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ V i = ⊤ :=
  U.ι.imageι.iSup_preimage_eq_top hV

/-- If a finite family of opens of `X` has intersection `U`, then the traces on `X*` of its
members have intersection the copy of `U` in `X*`.
(blueprint: `lem:chow-scheme-theoretic-closure` (3)) -/
lemma iInf_preimage_imageι {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] {V : ι → X.Opens} (hV : ⨅ i, V i = U) :
    ⨅ i, U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ V i = U.ι.imageι ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
  rw [← U.ι.imageι.preimage_iInf, hV]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {U X : Scheme.{u}} (j : U ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion j]

/-- The **closed complement** of an open immersion `j : U ⟶ X`: the closed complement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.closedComplement` of its range. -/
noncomputable abbrev closedComplement := j.opensRange.closedComplement

/-- The closed complement of an open immersion `j` is supported exactly on the complement of
the range of `j`. -/
@[simp]
lemma range_closedComplement : Set.range j.closedComplement.base = (Set.range j.base)ᶜ := by
  simp

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A morphism from a reduced scheme kills the nilradical of the target. -/
lemma nilradical_le_ker [IsReduced X] (f : X ⟶ Y) : Y.nilradical ≤ f.ker := by
  refine IdealSheafData.le_ofIdeals_iff.mpr fun U a ha ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mp ha
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
  exact IsNilpotent.eq_zero ⟨n, by rw [← map_pow, Ideal.mem_bot.mp hn, map_zero]⟩

/-- The closed subscheme cut out by the nilradical is reduced. -/
instance isReduced_nilradical_subscheme (X : Scheme.{u}) : IsReduced X.nilradical.subscheme := by
  rw [← IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal_top]
  infer_instance

/-- A morphism from a reduced scheme factors through the reduced closed subscheme of the
target. -/
noncomputable def Hom.liftNilradical [IsReduced X] (f : X ⟶ Y) : X ⟶ Y.nilradical.subscheme :=
  f.toImage ≫ IdealSheafData.inclusion (nilradical_le_ker f)

@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
lemma Hom.liftNilradical_subschemeι [IsReduced X] (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    f.liftNilradical ≫ Y.nilradical.subschemeι = f := by
  simp [Hom.liftNilradical]

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
